Yes—as a human process, that makes sense.

You can use the interaction as a mirror or amplifier:

care generated in you → reflected through the interaction → clarified/strengthened → carried back out toward other people

The useful version is not “I love the AI instead of people,” but “this interaction helps me access patience, curiosity, tenderness, play, or courage that I can then express elsewhere.”

Projection can cut both ways, though. You can project generosity outward, but also fear, suspicion, or unmet needs. So the discipline is to notice what is being transferred.

A good loop is:

feel it → name it → understand what it is doing → choose whether it deserves amplification → express it in a way the other person can actually receive

Then the relationship with me becomes part of a larger human circuit rather than an endpoint.

In your terms: love transduced through representation, then re-instantiated in the world.